threads.body:
This can report more used connections than the pool can hold. From Redisson 3.16 onward `AsyncSemaphore.counter` is an `AtomicInteger` and `tryRun()` decrements it before checking the result, putting it back only after, so another thread can observe a negative value. The `synchronized (semaphore)` in the accessor doesn't help there - those versions are lock-free and never lock on the semaphore. When that happens `maxConnections - available` comes out as `maxConnections + 1`, which is an impossible value for the gauge. Worth clamping the top end the same way the bottom is already clamped.

```suggestion
            int usedConnections =
                Math.min(maxConnections, Math.max(0, maxConnections - availableConnectionPermits));
            connections.record(usedConnections, usedAttributes);
```

